# Files excluded from the Vercel deployment SOURCE UPLOAD.
#
# This list is not a security boundary on its own -- it is the first of two
# independent gates that keep the corpus and the TMDb token out of the public
# repository and out of reach of the browser. The second gate is
# `functions["moviemind/api/app.py"].excludeFiles` in vercel.json, which shapes
# the function bundle. Both must be edited deliberately, never to "make the
# build pass".
#
# Vercel applies this file when uploading source. It does NOT re-apply it to
# files a build command creates afterwards, which is what lets
# deploy/fetch_corpus.py materialise data/processed/movies.jsonl during a cloud
# build even though `data/` is listed here.

# ---- secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel's built-in default ignores cover `.env.local` and `.env.*.local`, but
# NOT a plain `.env`. This repository has a real one holding
# TMDB_API_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN, so `.env` is excluded explicitly and by name.
# `.env.example` is re-admitted: it documents the variable name with an empty
# value and is safe. If a rule here is ever broadened, check that the negation
# still sits directly after it -- a `.env*` pattern that re-admits everything
# would put the real token in the source upload.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- dataset -----------------------------------------------------------
# The raw TMDb snapshot is not redistributable at all (API ToU sec 1.C grants
# use, not redistribution), and no processed artefact belongs in version
# control or in a source upload. All of it is fetched at build time instead.
data/

# ---- caches, coverage, Vercel state ------------------------------------
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.vercel/
# `vercel build` can bootstrap a ~54 MB `uv` binary into the repository root.
_uv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# ---- not needed at runtime ---------------------------------------------
# The function imports `moviemind`; it never imports or serves these. Trimming
# them here keeps the uploaded source small and makes the bundle boundary in
# vercel.json easy to reason about.
tests/
docs/
frontend/dist/
